 prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and August to September came in under 90% of normal in 37 of those 75 years, more than any other pair. In 2025 on the middle of the grids, January to February ran 64% of normal while May to June ran 148%. So far in 2026, January to February sits at 60% and June to July at 144%. Every grid had its driest year in 1964, with grid 26925 at 60% that year.</p>"}
